Below is a complete, ready‑to‑copy recipe for dealing with **missing icons** that a MapLibre GL JS style asks for.  
It uses the **MapLibre event system** so you don’t have to edit the style JSON manually – the map will automatically fetch (or synthesize) the missing image the first time it is needed, and then keep it around for the rest of the session.

---

## 1. Why the problem happens

When a style contains a `symbol` layer that references an image that has **not** been added to the map’s style image registry, MapLibre throws an error like:

```
Error: Image "my‑missing‑icon" not found.
```

In MapLibre GL JS (and in the upstream Mapbox GL JS) this situation is exposed as the **`styleimagemissing`** event.  
If you listen for that event you can:

1. **Detect** which image id is missing (`e.id`).
2. **Load** the image from wherever you keep your assets (static folder, CDN, data‑URI, generated canvas, etc.).
3. **Add** the image to the map (`map.addImage(e.id, image)`).
4. **Optionally** fall back to a placeholder if the real asset can’t be fetched.

Because the event fires **before** the layer is rendered, the newly‑added image will be used immediately – no need to reload the style or the page.

---

## 2. Minimal working example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>MapLibre – Missing‑icon handling</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; left:0; right:0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script>
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 1️⃣  Initialise the map (no icons added yet)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {
        // a tiny GeoJSON source with a single point
        points: {
          type: 'geojson',
          data: {
            type: 'FeatureCollection',
            features: [{
              type: 'Feature',
              geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.447303, 37.753574] },
              properties: {}
            }]
          }
        }
      },
      layers: [
        {
          id: 'points',
          type: 'symbol',
          source: 'points',
          layout: {
            // This icon does NOT exist yet → triggers styleimagemissing
            'icon-image': 'my-missing-icon',
            'icon-size': 1.5
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    center: [-122.447303, 37.753574],
    zoom: 12
  });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 2️⃣  Helper: fetch an image (returns a Promise that resolves with an ImageBitmap)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  function fetchImage(url) {
    return fetch(url)
      .then(r => {
        if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`);
        return r.blob();
      })
      .then(blob => createImageBitmap(blob));
  }

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 3️⃣  Event listener – the heart of the solution
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
    const missingId = e.id;               // e.g. "my-missing-icon"
    console.warn(`🛑 Icon "${missingId}" is missing – trying to load it…`);

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 3a️⃣  Decide where to look for the image.
    //      You can use any naming convention you like.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    const baseUrl = 'https://example.com/icons/'; // <-- change to your CDN / folder
    const url = `${baseUrl}${missingId}.png`;

    try {
      const imageBitmap = await fetchImage(url);
      // -----------------------------------------------------------------
      // 3b️⃣  Add the image to the style registry.
      //      The third argument (options) is optional – you can set sdf, pixelRatio, etc.
      // -----------------------------------------------------------------
      map.addImage(missingId, imageBitmap);
      console.info(`✅ Added "${missingId}" from ${url}`);
    } catch (err) {
      // -----------------------------------------------------------------
      // 3c️⃣  Fallback – use a generic placeholder so the map never stays blank.
      // -----------------------------------------------------------------
      console.error(`❌ Could not load "${missingId}" (${err.message}). Using fallback.`);
      const placeholderUrl = `${baseUrl}fallback.png`;
      try {
        const fallbackImg = await fetchImage(placeholderUrl);
        map.addImage(missingId, fallbackImg);
        console.info(`✅ Fallback "${missingId}" added.`);
      } catch (fallbackErr) {
        console.error(`🚨 Even the fallback failed: ${fallbackErr.message}`);
        // At this point you could either:
        //   • leave the layer without an icon (it will be invisible)
        //   • add a programmatic canvas‑generated icon (see section 4)
      }
    }
  });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 4️⃣  (Optional) Generate a simple canvas‑based placeholder on‑the‑fly.
  //      Useful if you don’t want to ship a PNG for every possible id.
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  function createCanvasIcon(color = '#ff0000', size = 32) {
    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    canvas.width = canvas.height = size;
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    ctx.fillStyle = color;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(size / 2, size / 2, size / 2 - 2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
    return canvas;
  }

  // Example of using the canvas fallback instead of a PNG:
  // map.on('styleimagemissing', (e) => {
  //   const canvas = createCanvasIcon('#00aaff');
  //   map.addImage(e.id, canvas);
  // });

</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What the code does

| Step | Explanation |
|------|-------------|
| **1️⃣ Initialise the map** | Loads a style that references `my-missing-icon`. No image is added yet, so the map will fire `styleimagemissing`. |
| **2️⃣ fetchImage()** | Small utility that returns an `ImageBitmap` (the format `map.addImage` expects). It works with any URL that returns a PNG/JPEG/WebP. |
| **3️⃣ styleimagemissing listener** | The core logic. When the event fires we: <br>• Build the URL for the missing icon (`${baseUrl}${missingId}.png`). <br>• Try to fetch it. <br>• If successful, add it with `map.addImage`. <br>• If the fetch fails, we fall back to a generic `fallback.png`. <br>• If even the fallback fails we optionally generate a canvas‑based icon (see 4️⃣). |
| **4️⃣ createCanvasIcon()** | Demonstrates a “no‑network” fallback: draw a simple colored circle on a `<canvas>` and add that as the missing image. This is handy for quick prototypes or when you want a deterministic placeholder without extra assets. |

