Below is a complete, ready‑to‑copy recipe for dealing with **missing icons** that a MapLibre GL JS style asks for.  
It uses the **MapLibre event system** so you don’t have to edit the style JSON manually – the map will automatically fetch (or synthesize) the missing image the first time it is needed, and then keep it in the style’s image cache for the rest of the session.

---

## 1. Why the problem happens

When a style contains a `symbol` layer that references an image that has **not** been added to the map’s style image registry, MapLibre throws an error like:

```
Error: Image "my‑missing‑icon" not found.
```

In MapLibre GL JS (and in the upstream Mapbox GL JS) this situation is exposed as the **`styleimagemissing`** event.  
If you listen for that event you can:

1. **Detect** which image id is missing (`e.id`).
2. **Load** the image from wherever you keep your assets (static URL, CDN, data‑uri, canvas, etc.).
3. **Add** the image to the map (`map.addImage(e.id, image)`).
4. Optionally **fallback** to a placeholder if the load fails.

Because the event fires **once per missing id**, you can safely add the same image multiple times – MapLibre will ignore duplicate `addImage` calls.

---

## 2. Minimal working example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – graceful missing‑icon handling</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; padding:0; height:100%; }
    #map { width:100%; height:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script>
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 1️⃣  Initialise the map (any style that references an unknown icon)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {
        "my-data": {
          type: "geojson",
          data: {
            type: "FeatureCollection",
            features: [
              {
                type: "Feature",
                geometry: { type: "Point", coordinates: [-122.447303, 37.753574] },
                properties: { name: "Missing icon example" }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      layers: [
        {
          id: "points",
          type: "symbol",
          source: "my-data",
          layout: {
            // This icon does NOT exist in the style yet → triggers the event
            "icon-image": "my‑missing‑icon",
            "icon-size": 1.2,
            "text-field": ["get", "name"],
            "text-offset": [0, 1.5],
            "text-anchor": "top"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    center: [-122.447303, 37.753574],
    zoom: 12
  });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 2️⃣  Helper: fetch an image (you can replace this with any async source)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  function fetchImage(url) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      const img = new Image();
      img.crossOrigin = "anonymous"; // needed for CDN images
      img.onload = () => resolve(img);
      img.onerror = (e) => reject(e);
      img.src = url;
    });
  }

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 3️⃣  Event listener – the core of the solution
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
    const missingId = e.id;               // e.g. "my‑missing‑icon"
    console.warn(`🛑 Icon "${missingId}" is missing – trying to load it…`);

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 3a️⃣  Decide where to get the image from.
    //      Here we assume a convention: icons live under /icons/<id>.png
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    const url = `/icons/${missingId}.png`;

    try {
      const img = await fetchImage(url);
      // MapLibre expects an HTMLImageElement, HTMLCanvasElement or ImageData
      map.addImage(missingId, img);
      console.info(`✅ Added "${missingId}" from ${url}`);
    } catch (err) {
      // -----------------------------------------------------------------
      // 3b️⃣  Fallback – use a generic placeholder (or a built‑in sprite)
      // -----------------------------------------------------------------
      console.error(`❌ Could not load "${missingId}" from ${url}`, err);
      const placeholderUrl = '/icons/default-placeholder.png';
      try {
        const placeholderImg = await fetchImage(placeholderUrl);
        map.addImage(missingId, placeholderImg);
        console.info(`⚡️ Fallback: used placeholder for "${missingId}"`);
      } catch (fallbackErr) {
        console.error(`💥 Even the fallback failed for "${missingId}"`, fallbackErr);
        // As a last resort you could draw a simple canvas‑based icon:
        const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
        canvas.width = canvas.height = 64;
        const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
        ctx.fillStyle = '#ff00ff';
        ctx.fillRect(0, 0, 64, 64);
        ctx.fillStyle = '#ffffff';
        ctx.font = 'bold 32px sans-serif';
        ctx.textAlign = 'center';
        ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';
        ctx.fillText('?', 32, 36);
        map.addImage(missingId, canvas);
        console.info(`🖼️  Created a tiny “?” icon for "${missingId}"`);
      }
    }
  });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 4️⃣  (Optional) Listen for generic errors – useful for debugging
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  map.on('error', (e) => {
    // e.error is the original Error object
    console.error('MapLibre error event:', e.error);
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What the code does

| Step | Explanation |
|------|-------------|
| **1️⃣ Initialise the map** | Loads a style that references an icon called `"my‑missing‑icon"` which we deliberately *don’t* add up‑front. |
| **2️⃣ fetchImage()** | Small wrapper that returns a `Promise<HTMLImageElement>` – you can replace it with `fetch()` + `createImageBitmap()`, a data‑uri, or any async source. |
| **3️⃣ styleimagemissing listener** | Fires **once per missing id**. Inside we: <br>• Build a URL based on a naming convention (`/icons/<id>.png`). <br>• Try to load the image. <br>• If successful, call `map.addImage(id, img)`. <br>• If the load fails, we fall back to a generic placeholder, and if that also fails we synthesize a tiny canvas‑based “?” icon. |
| **4️⃣ error listener** | Catches any other MapLibre errors (e.g., malformed style JSON) so you have a single place for logging. |

