## 4. Advanced patterns

### 4.1. Caching already‑tried ids

If you have a large number of potential icons (e.g., user‑generated names) you may want to avoid repeatedly trying to fetch a non‑existent file. A simple `Set` works:

```js
const triedIds = new Set();

map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
  if (triedIds.has(e.id)) return; // already attempted – skip
  triedIds.add(e.id);
  // …rest of the loading logic…
});
```

### 4.2. Batch loading for many missing icons

If you anticipate many missing icons at once (e.g., a style that references a whole sprite sheet that isn’t loaded), you can collect ids for a short debounce window and then request them in a single network call:

```js
let pending = new Set();
let debounceTimer = null;

map.on('styleimagemissing', (e) => pending.add(e.id));

function processPending() {
  const ids = Array.from(pending);
  pending.clear();
  // Example: request a zip of all needed icons from your server
  fetch('/batch-icons', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ icons: ids })
  })
  .then(r => r.json())
  .then(data => {
    data.forEach(({ id, dataUrl }) => {
      const img = new Image();
      img.onload = () => map.addImage(id, img);
      img.src = dataUrl;
    });
  })
  .catch(console.error);
}

// Debounce: wait 100 ms after the last missing‑icon event
map.on('styleimagemissing', () => {
  clearTimeout(debounceTimer);
  debounceTimer = setTimeout(processPending, 100);
});
```

### 4.3. Generating icons on the fly (e.g., colored circles)

Sometimes you don’t have a raster file at all; you just need a simple shape that varies by data property. You can generate a canvas and add it:

```js
function makeCircle(color, diameter = 32) {
  const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
  canvas.width = canvas.height = diameter;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
  ctx.fillStyle = color;
  ctx.beginPath();
  ctx.arc(diameter/2, diameter/2, diameter/2, 0, Math.PI*2);
  ctx.fill();
  return canvas;
}

// In the missing‑icon handler:
if (e.id.startsWith('circle-')) {
  const color = e.id.split('circle-')[1]; // e.g. "circle-ff0000"
  const img = makeCircle('#' + color);
  map.addImage(e.id, img);
}
```

