## 5. Full checklist for production‑ready handling

| ✅ Item | Why it matters |
|--------|----------------|
| **Listen to `styleimagemissing`** | Guarantees you only react to missing icons, not unrelated errors. |
| **Graceful fallback** | Guarantees the map never stays blank; a placeholder keeps UI usable. |
| **Cache successful & failed ids** | Prevents repeated network requests for the same missing asset. |
| **Error logging (both in the handler & via `map.on('error')`)** | Makes debugging easier in the field. |
| **Respect CORS** | Set `img.crossOrigin = 'anonymous'` when loading from a CDN. |
| **Avoid race conditions** | `addImage` is idempotent, but you may want to guard against rapid re‑adds if you debounce. |
| **Performance** | Load images lazily (only when needed) – the event system already does that. |
| **Accessibility** | If you generate a placeholder, consider adding a `text-field` fallback so screen‑readers still convey information. |
| **Testing** | Write a unit test that triggers `styleimagemissing` (e.g., by calling `map.triggerRepaint()` after removing an image) and asserts that `addImage` was called. |

