## 7️⃣ Minimal reproducible example (CommonJS → dynamic import)

```js
// file: demo.cjs
(async () => {
  // 1️⃣ Dynamically import the ESM entry point
  const { default: maplibregl } = await import('maplibre-gl');

  // 2️⃣ (Optional) Set up a tiny DOM with jsdom if you need to call Map constructor
  const { JSDOM } = require('jsdom');
  const dom = new JSDOM('<!DOCTYPE html><div id="map"></div>');
  global.window = dom.window;
  global.document = dom.window.document;
  global.navigator = { userAgent: 'node' };

  // 3️⃣ Create a map (will not actually render without a GL context)
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json',
    center: [0, 0],
    zoom: 2
  });

  console.log('MapLibre version:', maplibregl.version);
})();
```

Run it with:

```bash
node demo.cjs
```

You’ll see the version printed, proving that the import succeeded.

