`maplibre-gl` is now shipped as an **ES‑module**. In a plain Node environment you have to use the ESM loader (or import the UMD build that lives in `dist/`). The old CommonJS `require('maplibre‑gl')` entry point was removed, so it now throws.

Below is the **officially supported way** to load the library when you’re not using a bundler (Webpack, Rollup, Vite, etc.):

| Situation | What to do | Example |
|-----------|------------|---------|
| **Your project is already an ES‑module** (i.e. `package.json` has `"type": "module"` or you’re using `.mjs` files) | Use a normal static `import` | ```js\n// index.mjs or any .js file in a project with "type":"module"\nimport maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';\n\nconst map = new maplibregl.Map({\n  container: 'map',\n  style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json',\n  center: [0, 0],\n  zoom: 2\n});\n``` |
| **You are in a CommonJS file** (`.cjs` or a project without `"type":"module"`), but you still want to stay in CJS | Dynamically import the ESM bundle (Node ≥ 12.20 / 14.13) | ```js\n// index.cjs\n(async () => {\n  const { default: maplibregl } = await import('maplibre-gl');\n\n  const map = new maplibregl.Map({\n    container: 'map',\n    style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json',\n    center: [0, 0],\n    zoom: 2\n  });\n})();\n``` |
| **You really need a synchronous `require`** (e.g. legacy code that can’t be turned into async) | Pull in the **UMD** build that lives in `dist/` – it is a plain CommonJS file | ```js\n// index.cjs (or any .js when you *don’t* have \"type\":\"module\")\nconst maplibregl = require('maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.js');\n\nconst map = new maplibregl.Map({\n  container: 'map',\n  style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json',\n  center: [0, 0],\n  zoom: 2\n});\n``` |

